.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH murk-init 1  "init " 
.SH NAME
murk\-init \- Initialize a vault or reuse its existing key
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk init\fR [\fB\-\-vault\fR] [\fB\-\-reuse\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-separate\-key\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Initialize a vault or reuse its existing key
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fI<VAULT>\fR [default: .murk]
Vault filename
.TP
\fB\-\-reuse\-key\fR
When another vault in this directory already has a key stored on this machine, store that key for this vault too, without asking
.TP
\fB\-\-separate\-key\fR
When another vault in this directory already has a key stored on this machine, make a new key for this vault, without asking
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
